params.body:
Trends went on gentells.com only when a person approved them, and the card carried the full reading a model wrote (what is happening, why it matters, the semiotic read, the brand implication), plus a summary, linked trends with a sentence each, the layer graph and the shifts. Nobody screens that prose before it is public. This shows a trend by what the Observatory measured, and decides which trends go up by rule instead of by approval.

## Which trends go up

`siteTrendRows` (`packages/core/articles-store.mjs`) selects every trend that:
- is live (`liveInsightSql`: not lapsed, not superseded);
- has at least `TW_SITE_MIN_OBSERVED` (5) signals observed on a platform (`EVIDENCE_KIND_SQL = 'observed'`); press and reports do not count;
- has its newest observed signal at most `TW_SITE_FRESH_DAYS` (30) days old;
- is not taken off (`showcase_status = 'hidden'`).

A trend that goes quiet drops off by itself and comes back when it is seen again. A person can still take one off and put it back (`decideShowcase` hidden / approved). Order: the editors' `showcase_rank` first, then the most recently seen, then the most observed.

A new table `site_shown` records every id that actually went to the site, so the aliases of a folded trend keep only ids that were really public.

## What goes to the site

The projection (`packages/server/heavy.mjs`) now sends:
- the headline, tags, counts, evidence mix, recurrence and the signals;
- `observed` and `last_seen`.

It no longer sends:
- the four prose fields of the reading;
- the summary;
- the links;
- the graph;
- the shifts.

A signal's label is its own text (`raw_content`, else the url), no longer the classifier's note. The competitor check runs on the headline only, since nothing else written goes out.

## Studio and morning mail

- `siteTrendsOverview` gives each live trend its `observed`, `last_seen`, signal and source counts. It returns `pending: []` and the `rules`.
- `/site/trends` marks each trend `online`, `hidden` or `offline`.
- The morning curation run proposes nothing (`trends go on the site by rule`). `force` still works for a manual run.

## Deploy

This goes together with gentells-site (cards without prose, `last_seen`), gentells-studio and gentells-dashboard (online / taken off). The site's delete brake refuses a sync that would remove more than half of the current cards. If the new rules drop more than half of them, set `GENTELLS_MAX_DELETE_SHARE=1` on the site for one sync, then remove it.

## Tests

- `npm test`: 1608 of 1608. `tsc`: clean.
- New: `test/site-trends-by-rule.test.mjs` covers:
  - the three rules;
  - taken off and put back;
  - the order;
  - the projection carrying no model prose;
  - the old address of a folded trend;
  - the overview;
  - the morning mail.
- `test/projection-subgraph.test.mjs` is removed. The curated and site-mode blocks of `showcase.test.mjs` are removed. The fixtures follow the new label.
